  "question": {
    "text": "If $z=x-i y$ and $z^{\\frac{1}{3}}=p+i q$, then $\\frac{\\left(\\frac{x}{p}+\\frac{y}{q}\\right)}{\\left(p^2+q^2\\right)}$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "rO07L",
      "text": "\n1\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "nLcol",
      "text": "\n$-2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "7fqiN",
      "text": "\n2\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "5J8Tx",
      "text": "\n$-1$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$z=(p+i q)^3=p\\left(p^2-3 q^2\\right)-i q\\left(q^2-3 p^2\\right)$\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{x}{p}=p^2-3 q^2 \\& \\frac{y}{q}=q^2-3 p^2 \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\frac{x}{p}+\\frac{y}{q}}{\\left(p^2+q^2\\right)}=-2$",
    "image": null
  },
